(10. Supervisory Review Process) Tj
T*
(10.1 Individual Capital Guidance) Tj
T*
(The HKMA may set individual capital guidance above the minimum requirements for) Tj
T*
(institutions based on their risk profile and internal capital adequacy assessment.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(10.2 Pillar 2 Requirements) Tj
T*
(The supervisory review process \(Pillar 2\) requires banks to have robust internal capital) Tj
T*
(adequacy assessment processes and to hold capital against risks not covered under Pillar) Tj
T*
(1.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(11. Transitional Arrangements) Tj
T*
(11.1 Phase-in Period) Tj
T*
(The implementation of Basel III standards in Hong Kong follows transitional) Tj
T*
(arrangements, with full implementation by January 1, 2023.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(11.2 Grandfathering) Tj
T*
(Certain capital instruments issued before specific dates may be grandfathered during the) Tj
T*
(transition period.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(12. Enforcement) Tj
T*
(12.1 Supervisory Actions) Tj
T*
(The HKMA may take supervisory actions against institutions that fail to meet capital) Tj
T*
(adequacy requirements, including restrictions on dividend payments and business) Tj
T*
(activities.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(12.2 Remedial Measures) Tj
T*
(Institutions with capital deficiencies must submit and implement remedial plans to) Tj
T*
(restore compliance with capital requirements.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Conclusion) Tj
T*
(The HKMA's capital adequacy framework is designed to ensure the safety and soundness of) Tj
T*
(the Hong Kong banking system. By implementing Basel III standards with appropriate) Tj
T*
(enhancements, the framework promotes financial stability and protects depositors.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Issued by: Hong Kong Monetary Authority) Tj
T*
(Effective Date: January 1, 2023) Tj
T*
(Revision: SA-2.5) Tj
T*
() Tj
ET
